L’idea è questa:

Magic UI = reference/componenti belli
v0 = genera/adatta codice React + Tailwind
Cursor = integra nel tuo progetto vero

v0 genera UI React usando spesso convenzioni shadcn/ui + Tailwind, quindi è molto adatto a componenti moderni riusabili. Magic UI invece segue un processo compatibile con shadcn: installazione via shadcn CLI e componenti importabili nel progetto.

Workflow consigliato
1. Scegli il componente su Magic UI

Vai su Magic UI e scegli, per esempio:

Magic Card
Animated Gradient Border
Bento Grid
Marquee
Number Ticker
Shimmer Button

Salvati:

nome componente;
link;
screenshot;
codice se disponibile;
effetto che ti piace.
2. Vai su v0 e chiedi una versione compatibile con la tua app

Prompt tipo:

Create a React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 component inspired by Magic UI's [COMPONENT NAME].

Project context:
- React 18 + Vite + TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS v4
- Existing app has src/components/ui
- Use className overrides
- Use cn() from "@/lib/utils"
- Do not use Next.js APIs
- Do not use server components
- Do not use app router
- Do not use external paid libraries
- Keep the component reusable and isolated

Generate:
1. The component file
2. Required dependencies
3. Example usage
4. Notes for integration in an existing Vite app

Questo è fondamentale perché v0 tende spesso a ragionare in stile Next.js/shadcn. Tu devi dirgli chiaramente: Vite app, non Next.js.

3. Fai generare un componente “isolato”

Meglio chiedere file così:

src/components/ui/MagicCard.tsx

oppure:

src/components/ui/AnimatedCard.tsx

Non farlo intervenire subito su BookingRequestCard.

Prima devi avere un componente piccolo, testabile, riusabile.

4. Porta il codice in Cursor

Poi in Cursor dai questo prompt:

Integrate this new UI component into the existing project.

Rules:
- Do not change business logic.
- Do not change Supabase, TenantContext, hooks, routes, or database code.
- Keep the current props of existing feature components.
- Place reusable UI components in src/components/ui.
- Use cn() from src/lib/utils.ts.
- Avoid inline <style> blocks.
- Avoid new global CSS unless strictly necessary.
- Run npm run validate and npm run build.
5. Solo dopo lo applichi alle card vere

Quando il componente funziona, allora chiedi a Cursor:

Refactor BookingRequestCard to use the new AnimatedCard component.

Keep:
- same props
- same data
- same actions
- same status behavior
- same accessibility

Change only:
- visual layout
- spacing
- card structure
- hover/focus states
La cosa più importante

Non devi dire a v0:

Integrate Magic UI in my whole app

Devi dirgli:

Recreate this specific Magic UI-style component for my Vite React Tailwind app.
Attenzione alle dipendenze

Magic UI spesso usa:

framer-motion / motion
lucide-react
clsx
tailwind-merge
shadcn conventions

Nel tuo progetto lucide-react, clsx e tailwind-merge ci sono già. Se v0 propone nuove dipendenze, falle approvare da Cursor una per una, non installare tutto alla cieca.

Prompt super pronto per v0
I need a production-ready React component inspired by Magic UI, but adapted for an existing Vite + React 18 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 app.

Component to recreate:
[PASTE MAGIC UI COMPONENT NAME + LINK + SHORT DESCRIPTION]

Constraints:
- Do not use Next.js APIs.
- Do not use server components.
- Do not use app router.
- Use React 18 compatible code.
- Use TypeScript.
- Use Tailwind CSS classes.
- Use cn() from "@/lib/utils".
- Component must accept className.
- Component must be reusable inside src/components/ui.
- Avoid global CSS.
- Avoid inline <style> unless absolutely necessary.
- Keep dependencies minimal.
- If animation is needed, prefer CSS/Tailwind first; use framer-motion only if really necessary.

Output:
1. Full component code.
2. Required dependencies.
3. Example usage.
4. Integration notes for Cursor.
Prompt pronto per Cursor
You are integrating a v0-generated UI component into an existing React 18 + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 app.

Project rules:
- Do not modify Supabase, TenantContext, router, database, or business logic.
- Do not rewrite feature logic.
- Add reusable UI files only under src/components/ui.
- Use existing cn() from src/lib/utils.ts.
- Keep imports compatible with Vite.
- Avoid Next.js-specific imports.
- Avoid global CSS unless strictly required.
- Preserve existing component props when refactoring feature cards.
- Run npm run validate and npm run build.

Task:
1. Add the new component from v0.
2. Create one demo usage inside a low-risk admin component.
3. Replace only one existing card as a proof of concept.
4. Report changed files, dependencies added, and any visual conflicts found.

Quindi: Magic UI per scegliere, v0 per adattare/generare, Cursor per integrare con cautela.